  "recipes": {
    "grain": "preset manual = Sandow 1897 book stock, sigma .744% of luma per device pixel; inside the measured period range .30–1.41% (G.2.1: specimen/magazine .30–.45, book .74–1.41) and under the 1.35% cap. Zero mean, so the flat hex holds.",
    "rules": "gain is +0.10 iOS pt per edge = +0.055 period pt (the measured +0.05–0.06 on ½–¾ pt faces, G.3.2) × 1.8 period-to-iOS (G.3.3), on the two lines drawn from ATF nominal faces only (sub 1.2 and head's thin 1.2); hair and total are printed widths with no gain; none from 1 period pt up. Wander .03 / .015 pt rms, 1.33–16 pt wavelengths; no halo, pooling, breaks or bite.",
    "halftone": "tone map G.4.2 (Rec. 709 Y -> L* -> levels on the crop's P0.5/P99.5 -> a in [.04, 1] -> linear-light mix of stock and ink; no sepia matrix), then a 3.0 pt 45° Euclidean screen, dot area = a, no gain curve, 3 × 3 supersampled, 4-bit indexed PNG."
  },
  "use": {
    "grain": "the page (`rack`) only: never sheets, plates, fields, the dock, the status band or a photo band. Web: background-image image-set(grain-manual@2x.png 2x, grain-manual@3x.png 3x), background-size 72px 72px, repeat. Native: <Image source={require(\".../grain-manual.png\")} resizeMode=\"repeat\"> (Metro picks @2x / @3x) behind the page.",
    "rules": "each strip is pt[1] tall and repeats along x every 144pt; its first line's printed top is inkTopPt (1pt) below the strip's top, so place the strip 1pt above where the vector rule starts. Web: background image-set(... 2x, ... 3x) repeat-x, background-size 144px <pt[1]>px. Native: <Image resizeMode=\"repeat\" style={{ height: pt[1], alignSelf: \"stretch\" }}>. Draw the vector rule at the same widths until the strip loads (spec §11).",
    "halftone": "photographs only (the four bands and the thumbnail): `node textures.mjs halftone <in.png> <out.png> [pitchPt=3] [scale=3]` after sips has cropped and sized the plate. The photos job owns the plates and their PROVENANCE.json."
  },
